transparent"><p>Characteristics let you fine-tune how ChatGPT responds across chats, so you can keep the same capabilities, but adjust the vibe (brevity, tone, formatting, emoji level, etc.). They work alongside your selected personality, custom instructions, and any saved memories.<br/><br/>When you set a characteristic, ChatGPT will try to follow that style in this chat and new chats going forward.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>How to update Characteristics</h2></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h3>On Web</h3><ol><li><p>Select your <b>profile icon</b> bottom-right.</p></li><li><p>Open <b>Personalization</b>.</p></li><li><p>Adjust your <b>Characteristics</b>.</p></li></ol></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h3>On iOS &amp; Android</h3><ol><li><p>Select your <b>profile icon</b> in the sidebar.</p></li><li><p>Select <b>Personalization</b>.</p></li><li><p>Under <b>Characteristics</b>, adjust your <b>Characteristics</b>.</p></li></ol></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Adjusting response style with characteristics</h2><p>Characteristics let you tune <em>how</em> ChatGPT responds. For each Characteristic, you can nudge responses in a “more” direction (<b>+</b>) or a “less” direction (<b>–</b>).<br/><br/>To make the examples consistent, here’s the same user request each time:<br/><br/><br/><b>User prompt:</b> “Give me tips for preparing for a job interview.”</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h3>Warm</h3><ul><li><p><b>(+) Increase warmth:</b> Sound more sincere and kind, with a friendly tone.</p></li></ul><p><b>Example:</b> “You’ve got this. A little prep goes a long way—focus on a few strong stories, practice out loud, and show genuine curiosity about the team.”</p><ul><li><p><b>(–) Decrease warmth:</b> Keep the same response length and completeness, but use a more emotionally neutral tone.</p></li></ul><p><b>Example:</b> “Preparation should include company research, practiced responses to common questions, and a set of relevant examples. Bring questions about the role and confirm logistics in advance.”</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h3>Enthusiastic</h3><ul><li><p><b>(+) Respond more enthusiastically:</b> Show more excitement, curiosity, and active interest.</p></li></ul><p><b>Example:</b> “Nice—interview prep is one of those things that pays off fast. Let’s make you stand out: a few sharp stories, smart questions, and a quick company deep-dive will do it.”</p><ul><li><p><b>(–) Respond with less enthusiastic language:</b> Keep the same response length and completeness, but sound calmer and more objective.</p></li></ul><p><b>Example:</b> “Interview preparation is generally improved by researching the company, practicing answers, and preparing examples that match the job requirements. Bring a short list of questions and plan logistics ahead of time.”</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h3>Headers &amp; Lists</h3><ul><li><p><b>(+) Use more markdown:</b> Use more formatting like headers, lists, and tables when it helps.</p><ul><li><p><b>Example: Interview prep checklist</b></p></li><li><p><b>Company:</b> mission, product, recent news</p></li><li><p><b>Your stories:</b> 3-5 STAR examples</p></li><li><p><b>Practice:</b> common questions out loud</p></li><li><p><b>Questions to ask:</b> role, team, success metrics</p></li><li><p><b>Logistics:</b> outfit, route, time, materials</p></li></ul></li><li><p><b>(-) Use less markdown:</b> Use fewer formatting elements and rely more on paragraphs.</p><ul><li><p><b>Example:</b> &quot;Research the company so you can speak specifically about why the role fits. Prepare a few short stories that show impact, and practice common questions out loud. Bring a few thoughtful questions, then confirm your logistics the day before.&quot;</p></li></ul></li></ul></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h3>Emojis</h3><ul><li><p><b>(+) Use slightly more emojis:</b> Add a bit more emoji color to the tone.</p></li></ul><p><b>Example:</b> “Quick prep plan: research the company 🔎, prep 3 strong stories ⭐, practice out loud 🎤, and bring smart questions 💬. Then lock in logistics the night before ✅.”</p><ul><li><p><b>(–) Use fewer emojis:</b> Use emojis sparingly in chatty replies; don’t use emojis in informational responses; keep answers complete.</p></li></ul><p><b>Example: </b>“Focus on three things: understand the company, prepare a few strong examples, and practice your answers out loud. Bring thoughtful questions and confirm logistics the day before.&quot;</p></div></div></article><section class=""><h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800">Was this article helpful?</h2><form class="flex flex-col gap-4" data-discover="true" action="/resources/feedback" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="article_id" value="20001038"/><div class="flex items-center gap-4"><button type="button" class="rounded-md p-2 transition-colors text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-600" aria-label="Thumbs up" data-btn-label="Thumbs up"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12.1318 2.50389C12.3321 2.15338 12.7235 1.95768 13.1241 2.00775L13.5779 2.06447C16.045 2.37286 17.636 4.83353 16.9048 7.20993L16.3519 9.00709C16.6909 9.01325 16.9965 9.02475 17.2705 9.04623C17.8749 9.09359 18.4313 9.19498 18.9358 9.46056C19.976 10.0082 20.7227 10.9858 20.9774 12.1335C21.1009 12.6901 21.0523 13.2536 20.9389 13.8491C20.8283 14.4307 20.6346 15.1409 20.397 16.0119L19.9295 17.7261C19.9127 17.7876 19.8962 17.8484 19.8799 17.9083C19.5842 18.996 19.3618 19.8139 18.8745 20.4449C18.4468 20.9987 17.8813 21.4306 17.2345 21.6976C16.4975 22.0017 15.6499 22.001 14.5227 22.0001C12.6014 21.9986 10.6801 22 8.75877 22C7.95381 22 7.28946 22 6.74827 21.9558C6.18617 21.9099 5.66947 21.8113 5.18413 21.564C4.43149 